Chapter 9
Capital Structure and the Leverage Ratios
هيكل رأس المال ونسب الرافعة
Chapter 8 measured leverage from the income statement, as the magnifying effect of a fixed charge. This chapter measures the same thing from the balance sheet, as the proportion of the company financed by other people's money rather than the owners'. That proportion is the capital structure, and four ratios describe it.
The four are not four different facts. They are one fact — how much of the company is debt — expressed against four different denominators, and the exam expects you to move between them.
Figure F509-01 is your map.
Figure F509-01. Chapter 9 roadmap: one fact, four ratios, one decision.
