9.5  Putting the four ratios to work
YOUR TURN   Recompute the ratios after a decision
Figure F509-06 restates Orontes's balance sheet after it borrows $6,000,000 and uses it to repurchase shares. Compute the four ratios. Answers are at the end of the chapter.
Figure F509-06. Your turn: after a debt-funded buy-back (complete the blanks)
@table
Item | Amount
Total liabilities | 17,279,625
Total stockholders' equity | 14,392,975
Total assets | 31,672,600
Long-term debt | 12,000,000
Debt to equity | ________
Long-term debt to equity | ________
Debt to total assets | ________
Equity multiplier | ________
@end
Two habits separate a Level C answer from a Level B one.
State the direction and the size. "Debt to equity rises" is Level B. "Debt to equity rises from 0.55 to 1.20, and interest cover falls from 11.15 times to about 5 times, which is still within the covenant" is Level C.
Say who the change is for. The same movement reassures a shareholder expecting a higher return on equity and worries a bondholder whose cushion has halved. An answer that does not name the reader has not finished.
